eam":{"id":"15"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"3115035","displayName":"Christian Dvorak","shortName":"C. Dvorak"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"5080176","displayName":"Jiri Kulich","shortName":"J. Kulich"}}]},{"id":"401892732000000630","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":1,"homeScore":0,"text":"Tage Thompson Snap Shot saved by Joseph Woll","type":{"id":"506","text":"Shot","abbreviation":"shot-on-goal"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:01"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"2"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4024988","displayName":"Tage Thompson","shortName":"T. Thompson"},"type":"shooter"},{"athlete":{"id":"4271575","displayName":"Joseph Woll","shortName":"J. Woll"},"type":"saver"}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1845","fullName":"Xfinity Mobile Arena","address":{"city":"Philadelphia","state":"PA","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1845.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":18457,"officials":[{"fullName":"Jean Hebert","displayName":"Jean Hebert","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Jordan Samuels-Thomas","displayName":"Jordan Samuels-Thomas","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Tommy Hughes","displayName":"Tommy Hughes","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Kilian McNamara","displayName":"Kilian McNamara","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Christian Dvorak lifts Flyers past Sabres 4-3 as Matvei Michkov extends point streak","description":"— Christian Dvorak and Jamie Drysdale each had a goal and an assist, and Matvei Michkov extended his point streak to five games with two assists as the Philadelphia Flyers beat the scuffling Buffalo Sabres 4-3 on Tuesday night.","story":"PHILADELPHIA -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3115035/christian-dvorak\">Christian Dvorak</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697387/jamie-drysdale\">Jamie Drysdale</a> each had a goal and an assist, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5149170/matvei-michkov\">Matvei Michkov</a> extended his point streak to five games with two assists as the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/phi/philadelphia-flyers\">Philadelphia Flyers</a> beat the scuffling <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/buf/buffalo-sabres\">Buffalo Sabres</a> 4-3 on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3114757/travis-sanheim\">Travis Sanheim</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4392072/owen-tippett\">Owen Tippett</a> also scored for the Flyers. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4271575/joseph-woll\">Joseph Woll</a> made 16 saves. \n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4024988/tage-thompson\">Tage Thompson</a> scored his 13th goal and added an assist for Buffalo, which is 0-4-1 in its last five games. <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4378656/mattias-samuelsson\">Mattias Samuelsson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/5080176/jiri-kulich\">Jiri Kulich</a> also scored, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3654006/alex-lyon\">Alex Lyon</a> stopped 29 shots. \n\n\r\n              Dvorak scored at 5:23 of the third period, snapping a shot from the right circle over Lyon's left shoulder to give Philadelphia a 4-3 lead.\n\n\r\n              Dvorak also made a deft cross-ice pass to Sanheim on the first shift of the third, and the defenseman wristed it past Lyon at the 29-second mark for his fourth goal of the season. \n\n\r\n              Drysdale scored the Flyers' first goal at 6:39 of the second, snapping a feed from Michkov past Lyon to tie the score at 1. Drysdale later set up Tippett with a seeing-eye pass through several Buffalo defenders for a goal.\n\n\r\n              Michkov became the first Flyers player with four five-game point streaks before age 22 since Simon Gagne in 2001.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Sabres: Continue a six-game trip, their longest of the season, Thursday in Washington.\n\n\r\n              Flyers: Begin a three-game trip Thursday at Ottawa.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-18T15:13:16Z"}}